WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.380
You know what?

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.300
We ended season 5 on a HUGE cliffhanger.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.980
You want to find out whether, you know, Captain Holt becomes a commissioner or not,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.880
I promise you, that will be answered in the first episode.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.330
We will find out and then now that, you know,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.760
Jake and Amy are married, we're gonna see where this relationship goes. You know what I'm saying?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.970
And I'm ready for more high jinks, more stuff with the crew.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.600
It's just gonna be insane. More– more and better.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.840
All of us are really thrilled to be on NBC. I think

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.960
we've always had those roots in our show because they produced our show from the get-go.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.860
I am personally really excited about being able to say bad words and then have them be bleeped out?

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.860
Yeah.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.740
I think that's just, like (chef's kiss)

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.900
Yeah, it just feels... it's– it's beyond. I mean, it was such a, like, unexpected,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.000
surprising outcome to that whole two days.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:08.500
And yeah, like, somebody said they've always produced our show so it's a bit of, like, 'going home' in a sense.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.180
It's great. We're so excited, and they're excited, and everybody's excited.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.140
Excitement abounds.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:16.900
Abound.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.680
Abound

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.140
The new season holds many fun stories.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.480
(laughs)

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.880
Obviously, we're gonna pay off the cliffhanger with Captain Holt.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.960
We're gonna find out whether or not he got the big promotion as commissioner.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.920
We're gonna see what married life holds for Jake and Amy.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.500
We're gonna see Rosa's

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:39.869
newfound love life continue.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:48.029
I'm sure we're gonna see Charles, infatuated with food and being slightly weird, but lovable.

00:01:48.029 --> 00:01:49.480
(laughs)

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.480
It's gonna be good. We're excited. There's a lot of fun stories coming.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.600
I would hope that we would have some amazing guest stars,

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.900
as well as the continuing foibles of our squad.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.360
Nothing is... If it's not broke, we're not gonna fix it. We're a lot of the same

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.319
I think that

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:12.720
NBC now allows us to, like, use bleeps for, like,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.700
(whispers) profanity.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.320
Not that– that's not what we're pushing here, but like sometimes, you just gotta, just– you gotta say it.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.700
More of the same, like, we're really excited.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.560
Oh my god, you know it's weird because I'm a comic-con vet.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.400
I've been here since, like,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.569
2010, with the

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:36.609
Expendables and all three of them, and and then all the I hosted the Netflix panel last year but to be back because my show

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:41.139
is now on NBC. We're back to life we're back from the dead.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.540
It's absolutely amazing and we took a bus down here from LA and it's been a party the whole time.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.920
(sings in harmony)

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.170
I think our panel is gonna be really fun. Yeah, later. I think that'll be really fun

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:00.509
Our fans usually have really great, weird, cool questions during Q&amp;As.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.452
So I'm psyched for that.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.780
And I heard there was, like, a line for our panel earlier.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.180
Oh, that's cool.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.340
That's cool.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.360
There's also, and we're gonna do a giveaway of, like, signed,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:18.980
like, scripts and DVDs and so I think people are gonna be excited to do that Brooklyn 99 trivia, that kind of thing.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.060
We had a, you know,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:25.200
the kind of a sad last day in season five weren't sure if we were gonna get picked up,

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.400
and we're like,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.970
"But even if we don't, I'm sure maybe Hulu or Netflix will do it."

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.000
And then when that didn't happen, there was this feeling of,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.000
"Wow, this is really over. This is done."

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.860
And then suddenly, you know, the Twitter and social media went

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.440
ballistic and suddenly we were saved.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.500
It was like, you know being brought back from the dead, it was like, "Clear! STAT!"

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.040
It was just amazing, really good.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.820
We're ecstatic to have a new lease on life.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.369
You know, we thought that we weren't gonna be making the show anymore and NBC saved us.

00:03:58.359 --> 00:04:00.809
Like, so many nights off the round table.

00:04:02.049 --> 00:04:09.509
Because, you know what? The internet brought this thing back. The internet loves Brooklyn 99, and the internet runs Comic Con.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:12.420
I mean, this is where the buzz happens. This is where you find out

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:17.669
who's who, what's what, what's cool over the next year and it's all about blogging,

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:20.848
it's all about putting this stuff down and, you know,

00:04:20.849 --> 00:04:25.649
it's about the Facebook and Twitter and Instagram, and this is what it is.

00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:27.680
And it's funny how I saw

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:34.660
someone cosplayed me as Terry Jeffords with the suspenders and tie, and I retweeted it,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.240
I'm going, "Only at comic-con."

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.580
It's incredible. We didn't think we'd be around, let alone at comic-con. So we're thrilled.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:46.340
We're thrilled with the outpouring of love and support we've had from our fans. Thank you very much.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.340
I mean just just the outpouring, the unapologetic

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.029
fandom here is the best.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:58.000
I was a nerd when I was a kid. I was into Stephen King and horror comics and and I was as passionate as

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.920
many– everyone here is about their particular show. So I feel at home.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.680
It's incredible. I mean

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.660
We've done promotion for the show before over the last few seasons, but this is out of this world.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.619
I didn't know how huge, I mean, I'd read about it,

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.900
I heard about it, but I just thought it was kind of like in one building or something.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.900
Oh my god, the city of San Diego.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:27.840
Comic-con has taken over the whole city. It's amazing. We had no idea. Well, we met the people from Doctor Know.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.480
Doctor Who.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.480
Doctor Who?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.640
Doctor Know Who.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.650
(laughs) Who knows?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.509
But here's the deal we're both huge fans of a show called Broadchurch, in which

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:46.299
the people who are behind this show are all– and we were we were both like, "Oh my god,

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:52.570
We love you," and this is what's cool: they said, "we love Brooklyn 99." It was so cool. That was really great

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.900
I actually said to her, "I can–" Amanda, I think her name is?

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.600
The lead? I can't remember her name.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.400
Be careful.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:04.150
Yeah, here I go stepping right into it some more I said, "Oh, I'm so excited for your role in Doctor Know!"

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.120
But I was thinking about Broadchurch. I felt like a big dummy, but anyway.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.240
So you planted the seed, thanks a lot.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:11.960
We have no idea.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.140
We're waiting. We don't know we haven't read a script yet

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.340
But I'm assuming it's gonna be very good.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.550
(laughs)

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:25.930
I don't think it'll be dramatically different, if it's different at all. I'm not sure. I haven't– we have not seen a script.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.120
We don't know Dan Goor and his guys are–

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.280
and Andy, they're all putting it together at this point. They're a little tight-lipped.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:36.360
We'll have our first table read on the 8th of August.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.280
August 8th, yeah

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:42.820
And then we'll then we'll know a little more. But NBC is old home for me,

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.400
I mean, my dad was on NBC forever

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:50.109
And I was on NBC for a few years years before you were born,

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.120
I imagine, but at any rate–

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.899
So we're– I'm thrilled to be back and and we're just thrilled to– we're thrilled to be moving on. Fantastic.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.500
We've been welcomed with open arms.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.960
Yes we have.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:02.720
And we're very happy about it.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.080
Ten out of ten.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.860
"Ten out of ten," nailed it.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.860
A hundred percent.

